  "subdivision_of_building": "Exterior of Ground Floor by entrance of 73 Great Eastern Street.",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "We are proposing the installation of two awnings at 73 Great Eastern Street, EC2A 3HU. The two awnings will be installed on the storefront to provide weather protection for customers and enhance the aesthetic appeal of the building. \n\nThe awnings will be mounted above the entrance on Great Eastern Street west-northwest facing. Each awning will measure approximately 2.4 meters in width with a 2-meter projection. The awnings will be made of waterproof acrylic of a muted or appropriate colour and attached to treated plywood. \n\nThe awnings are intended to provide practical weather protection for customers and passersby, enhance the visual appeal of the façade, and align with the overall branding of the premises. The awnings will not obstruct pedestrian walkways or neighbouring properties. The installation of the awnings is designed to blend with the current architectural style of the building and the surrounding area. There will be no significant visual or environmental impact on the neighbouring properties. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>"
